rc/style.css`"},"980":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-69","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#module-map-measured","content":"1,376"},"981":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-70","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#module-map-measured","content":"Entire OS stylesheet — glass UI, wallpapers, animations"},"982":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-71","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#boot-sequence","content":"`main.ts` renders the boot screen with a progress ring (SVG\n`stroke-dashoffset` animated from 326 → 0) and a status line."},"983":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-72","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#boot-sequence","content":"Five staged steps run with randomized pacing: kernel → filesystem mount →\nwindow manager → applications → shell services."},"984":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-73","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#boot-sequence","content":"Subsystems are constructed: `FileSystem` (hydrated from localStorage or\nseeded), `ProcessManager`, `WindowManager` (bound to `#windows-layer`),\n`AppRegistry` (8 apps registered)."},"985":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-74","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#boot-sequence","content":"The desktop shell is built (icons, taskbar, start menu, context menu,\nlock screen, clock), the boot screen fades out, and the login chime plays."},"986":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-75","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#eventbus--the-communication-backbone","content":"Every subsystem communicates exclusively through named events; modules never\nimport each other directly. The bus provides:"},"987":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-76","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#eventbus--the-communication-backbone","content":"**Typed `on` / `once`** subscriptions with unsubscribe handles"},"988":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-77","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#eventbus--the-communication-backbone","content":"**Error isolation** — a throwing handler never breaks other listeners"},"989":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-78","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#eventbus--the-communication-backbone","content":"**History** — the last 200 emissions are kept for telemetry/debugging"},"990":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-79","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#eventbus--the-communication-backbone","content":"**`emitAsync`** — microtask-queued emission"},"991":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-80","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#eventbus--the-communication-backbone","content":"Well-known events: `boot:*`, `window:*`, `process:*`, `fs:changed`,\n`theme:changed`, `audio:volume`, `app:*`."},"992":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-81","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#processmanager","content":"Every window is backed by a `Process` record (PID, name, icon, state,\nstarted-at, CPU/mem telemetry). PIDs start at 100. `ps` and `kill` operate\non this table; the System Monitor and taskbar read from it. A `tick()`\nrandom-walk updates telemetry so the monitor looks alive."},"993":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-82","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#windowmanager","content":"Windows are DOM elements with chrome built by the manager — apps never touch\nthe titlebar or controls. Features:"},"994":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-83","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#windowmanager","content":"Drag via titlebar (`mousedown` + window-level `mousemove`/`mouseup`)"},"995":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-84","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#windowmanager","content":"8 resize handles (`n`, `s`, `e`, `w` + corners), 320×220 minimum size"},"996":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-85","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#windowmanager","content":"Focus raises z-index; the focused window gets an accent glow"},"997":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-86","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#windowmanager","content":"Maximize toggles to full-layer geometry; minimize animates out"},"998":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-87","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#windowmanager","content":"Cascading default placement; `singleInstance` apps reuse their window"},"999":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-88","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#filesystem--posix-lite","content":"Path resolution supports absolute and relative paths with `.` and `..`\n(rejecting escapes above root with `EPERM`)."},"1000":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-89","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#filesystem--posix-lite","content":"`resolve(path, cwd)` normalizes; every operation throws typed `FSError`s:\n`ENOENT`, `EISDIR`, `ENOTDIR`, `EEXIST`, `EPERM`, `EINVAL`."},"1001":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-90","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#filesystem--posix-lite","content":"Recursive ops: `mkdirp`, `removeRecursive`, `copy`, `move`, `tree`."},"1002":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-91","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#filesystem--posix-lite","content":"Persistence: the tree serializes to `localStorage` (`aurora.fs.v1`) on\nevery mutation and rehydrates at boot; `wipe()` restores the seed image."},"1003":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-92","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#filesystem--posix-lite","content":"The default image ships a `/home/user` with Desktop, Documents, Pictures,\nMedia and Projects plus system dirs (`/bin`, `/etc`, `/tmp`, `/var`)."},"1004":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-93","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#shell-interpreter-pure","content":"`commands.ts` is fully DOM-free: `runCommand(line, shell, fs, ctx)` takes a\n`Shell` (print callbacks + cwd) and works in Node. Highlights:"},"1005":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-94","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#shell-interpreter-pure","content":"**Redirection** — `>` and `>>` captured through a proxy shell"},"1006":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-95","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#shell-interpreter-pure","content":"**Quoting** — `tokenize()` honors double quotes"},"1007":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-96","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#shell-interpreter-pure","content":"**Command context** — `ps`/`kill`/`open`/`apps`/`history`/`shutdown` bind\nto the live process table and app registry"},"1008":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-97","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#shell-interpreter-pure","content":"**35+ commands** — full reference in the user guide"},"1009":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-98","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#audio--no-files-all-synthesis","content":"`SoundSystem.ts` lazily creates a single `AudioContext` on the first user\ngesture (autoplay policy). Every effect is an oscillator + gain envelope:\nboot chime (three rising notes), UI click, window open/close sweeps, error\nbuzz, unlock notification. The Settings app can disable it entirely."},"1010":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-99","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#theming--persistence","content":"Settings live in `localStorage` (`aurora.settings.v1`)."},"1011":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-100","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#theming--persistence","content":"Themes map to CSS custom properties (`--acc`, `--acc2`, `--bg`) applied on\n`&lt;html&gt;data-theme>`; the light theme flips text/border tokens."},"1012":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-101","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#theming--persistence","content":"Five wallpapers are pure CSS — the default \"Aurora\" animates two blurred\ngradient blobs with a 18s/22s drift loop (respects `prefers-reduced-motion`)."},"1013":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-102","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#testing-strategy","content":"The core is DOM-free and unit-tested: `npm test` bundles the pure modules\nwith esbuild and runs **34 assertions** covering the EventBus (emit, once,\nunsubscribe, error isolation), FileSystem (paths, CRUD, error codes,\nrecursive ops) and shell (echo, cd/pwd, ls, redirection, cat, mkdir, touch,\nwc, unknown-command handling)."},"1014":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture-103","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os/architecture#testing-strategy","content":"*Next: User guide — commands, shortcuts, apps · Overview*"},"1015":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os","type":"page","content":"◈ Aurora","breadcrumbs":["Catalog","📁 Projects","◈ Aurora"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os"},"1016":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os-0","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os","content":"**A complete operating system running in your browser.** Aurora is a from-scratch desktop environment — window manager, virtual"},"1017":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os-1","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os#-aurora","content":"◈ Aurora"},"1018":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os-2","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os#-what-is-aurora","content":"🎯 What is Aurora?"},"1019":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os-3","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os#-feature-matrix","content":"✨ Feature matrix"},"1020":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os-4","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os#-quick-start","content":"🚀 Quick start"},"1021":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os-5","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os#️-first-steps-inside-the-os","content":"🖱️ First steps inside the OS"},"1022":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os-6","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os#-links","content":"🔗 Links"},"1023":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os-7","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os#-aurora","content":"<a class=\"tests-cta\" href=\"./tests\">🧪 View animated test results — 56/56 →</a>"},"1024":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os-8","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os#-aurora","content":"**A complete operating system running in your browser.**"},"1025":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os-9","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os#-aurora","content":"Aurora is a from-scratch desktop environment — window manager, virtual\nfile system, shell, and eight applications — written entirely in TypeScript\nwith **zero runtime dependencies**. No frameworks, no server, no build\nartifacts at runtime: the kernel boots, renders, and persists entirely in\nyour browser tab."},"1026":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os-10","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os#-aurora","content":"> *\"Your browser is now your computer.\"*"},"1027":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os-11","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os#-what-is-aurora","content":"Most \"web OS\" demos are a single window with buttons. Aurora is an actual\nsystem: it boots through an animated kernel sequence, owns a process table,\nmultiplexes windows with full drag/resize/minimize/maximize semantics, hosts\na POSIX-flavored virtual filesystem with persistence, and ships an\ninteractive shell with **36+ commands** — all implemented from scratch."},"1028":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os-12","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os#-what-is-aurora","content":"The entire project is **\\~4,500 lines** of hand-written TypeScript + CSS\n(3,118 lines of TS across 16 modules, 1,376 lines of CSS), with **no\nexternal runtime dependencies**."},"1029":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os-13","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os#-feature-matrix","content":"Layer"},"1030":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os-14","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os#-feature-matrix","content":"Capabilities"},"1031":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os-15","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os#-feature-matrix","content":"🧠 **Kernel**"},"1032":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os-16","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os#-feature-matrix","content":"Animated boot sequence with progress ring · typed EventBus (pub/sub, once, history, error isolation) · PID process table with telemetry · settings subsystem · localStorage persistence"},"1033":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os-17","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os#-feature-matrix","content":"🪟 **Window manager**"},"1034":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os-18","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os#-feature-matrix","content":"Drag by titlebar · 8-direction resize handles · minimize / maximize / focus · cascading placement · z-order management · glassmorphism chrome · open/close animations · taskbar integration"},"1035":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os-19","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os#-feature-matrix","content":"📂 **Virtual filesystem**"},"1036":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os-20","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os#-feature-matrix","content":"POSIX-inspired tree · absolute + relative paths with `.` / `..` resolution · `mkdir -p`, recursive `rm -r`, `cp`, `mv` · proper error codes (`ENOENT`, `EISDIR`, `EEXIST`, `EPERM`, `ENOTDIR`) · human-readable sizes · localStorage persistence"},"1037":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os-21","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os#-feature-matrix","content":"⌨️ **Terminal & shell**"},"1038":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os-22","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os#-feature-matrix","content":"36+ commands (incl. `find`) · command history (↑/↓) · Tab path completion · output redirection (`>` / `>>`) · ANSI color rendering · `neofetch`, `fortune`, `sudo` (you are root) · pure interpreter, fully unit-tested"},"1039":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os-23","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os#-feature-matrix","content":"📱 **Applications**"},"1040":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os-24","page_id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/aurora-os#-feature-matrix","content":"Files · Terminal · Editor (Ctrl+S) · Calculator · Paint (PNG export) · System Monitor (live CPU/memory graphs) · Settings · About"},"1041":{"id":"/docs/projects/aurora-os-25","p