:"Enumerates every combination of a charset up to `maxlen`:"},"1359":{"id":"/docs/projects/cybersec-tools/hashsleuth-54","page_id":"/docs/projects/cybersec-tools/hashsleuth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/cybersec-tools/hashsleuth#mode-3-brute-masked-brute-force","content":"**Parallelization:** workers stride the flat index space (`i = w; i += workers`)\nacross every position and length; each worker decodes its index into charset\ndigits (base-N counter)."},"1360":{"id":"/docs/projects/cybersec-tools/hashsleuth-55","page_id":"/docs/projects/cybersec-tools/hashsleuth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/cybersec-tools/hashsleuth#mode-3-brute-masked-brute-force","content":"**Search-space guard:** if `charset^len > 100,000,000` the tool aborts that\nlength with a clear message instead of exhausting CPU."},"1361":{"id":"/docs/projects/cybersec-tools/hashsleuth-56","page_id":"/docs/projects/cybersec-tools/hashsleuth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/cybersec-tools/hashsleuth#mode-3-brute-masked-brute-force","content":"> **Note:** brute force grows exponentially — with a 26-character charset the\n> 100M search-space cap is already exceeded at length 6 (26⁶ = 308M), so the\n> practical limit is \\~5 characters. Prefer a good wordlist (dictionary mode)."},"1362":{"id":"/docs/projects/cybersec-tools/hashsleuth-57","page_id":"/docs/projects/cybersec-tools/hashsleuth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/cybersec-tools/hashsleuth#algorithm-auto-detection","content":"When `--algo` is omitted, the hash length selects the algorithm:"},"1363":{"id":"/docs/projects/cybersec-tools/hashsleuth-58","page_id":"/docs/projects/cybersec-tools/hashsleuth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/cybersec-tools/hashsleuth#algorithm-auto-detection","content":"Length"},"1364":{"id":"/docs/projects/cybersec-tools/hashsleuth-59","page_id":"/docs/projects/cybersec-tools/hashsleuth","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/cybersec-tools/has