onitor","content":"**eBPF endpoint security agent for Linux — detect ransomware behaviour, respond at the kernel edge.** Talus traces `execve`, `openat`, `connect`, `accept`,..."},"4139":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-1","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#️-talus","content":"🛰️ Talus"},"4140":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-2","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#-what-it-does","content":"🎯 What it does"},"4141":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-3","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#️-architecture","content":"⚙️ Architecture"},"4142":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-4","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#-quick-start","content":"🚀 Quick start"},"4143":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-5","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#️-usage","content":"🖥️ Usage"},"4144":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-6","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#️-the-ransomware-heuristic","content":"🛡️ The ransomware heuristic"},"4145":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-7","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#-licensing--editions","content":"◆ Licensing & Editions"},"4146":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-8","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#-project-layout","content":"📦 Project layout"},"4147":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-9","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#-requirements","content":"🔧 Requirements"},"4148":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-10","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#️-talus","content":"<a class=\"tests-cta\" href=\"./tests\">🧪 View animated test results — 95/95 →</a>"},"4149":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-11","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#️-talus","content":"**eBPF endpoint security agent for Linux — detect ransomware behaviour, respond at the kernel edge.**"},"4150":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-12","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#️-talus","content":"Talus traces `execve`, `openat`, `connect`, `accept`, `sendto` and `recvfrom`\nsyscalls at the kernel level using eBPF tracepoints, streams events into\nuserspace through per-CPU perf buffers, and surfaces them in a live terminal\nFrankenTUI — while continuously scoring per-process file-open rates against\na sliding window to flag ransomware-style mass file access, and automatically\n`SIGKILL`-ing offending processes."},"4151":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-13","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#️-talus","content":"> **Project status:** production-quality Rust + eBPF engineering showcase,\n> shipped with a commercial licensing system — Ed25519-signed keys and a\n> live activation backend on Cloudflare Workers + D1 (free tier)."},"4152":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-14","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#-what-it-does","content":"Capability"},"4153":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-15","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#-what-it-does","content":"Description"},"4154":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-16","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#-what-it-does","content":"**Kernel-level tracing**"},"4155":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-17","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#-what-it-does","content":"`execve` and `openat` tracepoints attached on every online CPU"},"4156":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-18","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#-what-it-does","content":"**Verifier-safe kernel code**"},"4157":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-19","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#-what-it-does","content":"Userspace pointers read exclusively via `bpf_probe_read_user` — never dereferenced"},"4158":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-20","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#-what-it-does","content":"**Zero-copy event pipeline**"},"4159":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-21","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#-what-it-does","content":"Fixed-size `ProcessEvent` records streamed through per-CPU `PerfEventArray` buffers"},"4160":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-22","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#-what-it-does","content":"**Live FrankenTUI**"},"4161":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-23","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#-what-it-does","content":"7-panel cyberpunk interface: events, processes, network, files, extensions, alerts, heatmap"},"4162":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-24","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#-what-it-does","content":"**Sliding-window heuristic**"},"4163":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-25","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#-what-it-does","content":"1-second rolling window per PID; alerts when a process exceeds the configured open rate"},"4164":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-26","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#-what-it-does","content":"**Multiple output modes**"},"4165":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-27","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#-what-it-does","content":"Human TUI, newline-delimited JSON, plain text log, and a built-in self-diagnostic"},"4166":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-28","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#-what-it-does","content":"**Lost-event accounting**"},"4167":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-29","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#-what-it-does","content":"Perf-buffer overruns are counted and reported, never silently dropped"},"4168":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-30","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#-what-it-does","content":"**Single static binary**"},"4169":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-31","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#-what-it-does","content":"Full LTO, `panic = \"abort\"`, symbol-stripped release profile"},"4170":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-32","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#️-architecture","content":"Kernel-side eBPF programs capture every `execve`/`openat` into a compact\n`ProcessEvent` record pushed into a `PerfEventArray`. A dedicated userspace\nreader thread opens one perf buffer per CPU, decodes events, and forwards\nthem over an MPSC channel to the monitor core, which feeds a 1-second sliding\nwindow per PID and emits alerts when the threshold is crossed."},"4171":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-33","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#️-architecture","content":"See the full architecture for the complete design."},"4172":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-34","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#️-usage","content":"**TUI keys:** `q` / `Esc` / `Ctrl+C` quit · `p` pause/resume · `c` clear log ·\n`↑/↓`/`j/k` scroll · `PgUp`/`PgDn` faster · `Home`/`End` jump."},"4173":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-35","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#️-the-ransomware-heuristic","content":"> **For every PID, keep a 1-second sliding window of `openat` calls. If the\n> window contains ≥ N opens (default 50), emit an alert.**"},"4174":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-36","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#️-the-ransomware-heuristic","content":"Sliding window, not a rate counter — bursts are caught as reliably as steady streams"},"4175":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-37","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#️-the-ransomware-heuristic","content":"Per-process isolation — no cross-process false positives"},"4176":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-38","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#️-the-ransomware-heuristic","content":"`--alert-threshold 0` disables the heuristic entirely"},"4177":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-39","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#-licensing--editions","content":"Talus ships in two editions. **Community** is free and MIT-licensed; the\n**Enterprise** features (auto-kill, web dashboard, Kafka, ClickHouse,\nMemGraph, C FFI) are unlocked by a paid license key."},"4178":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-40","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#-licensing--editions","content":"Layer"},"4179":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-41","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#-licensing--editions","content":"Implementation"},"4180":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-42","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#-licensing--editions","content":"**Signed keys**"},"4181":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor-43","page_id":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/projects/talus-process-monitor#-licensing--editions","content":"`base64(payload).base64(Ed25519 signature)` — the binary embeds the *public* key only; the signing key never leaves the owner's machine"},"4182":{"id":"/docs/projects/talus-proces